# Greensleeves - ChordPro feature showcase
# PUBLIC DOMAIN: English traditional, 16th century. Melody + words long out of copyright.
# Demonstrates: {define} chord diagrams, {start_of_tab} block, chorus recall,
# comments, and how to transpose. Substitutes the (equally traditional) rich
# example; every {start_of_*} has a matching {end_of_*}.

{title: Greensleeves}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: Am}
{time: 6/8}
{tempo: 90}

# Define fingerings for the two less-obvious chords (low E -> high E; 0=open, x=muted).
{define: Am base-fret 1 frets x 0 2 2 1 0}
{define: E7 base-fret 1 frets 0 2 0 1 0 0}

{comment: Intro (simplified Am arpeggio)}
{start_of_tab}
e|-------0-------0-----|
B|-----1-------1-------|
G|---2-------2---------|
A|-0-------0-----------|
{end_of_tab}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A[Am]las, my [C]love, you [G]do me [Em]wrong
To [Am]cast me [E7]off dis-[Am]cour-teous-ly
For [Am]I have [C]loved you [G]oh so [Em]long
De-[Am]light-ing [E7]in your [Am]com-pa-ny
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
{comment: Chorus}
[C]Green-sleeves was [G]all my [Em]joy
[Am]Green-sleeves was [E7]my de-[Am]light
[C]Green-sleeves was my [G]heart of [Em]gold
And [Am]who but my [E7]la-dy [Am]Green-sleeves
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [Am]have been [C]read-y [G]at your [Em]hand
To [Am]grant what-[E7]ev-er [Am]you would crave
I [Am]have both [C]wa-ged [G]life and [Em]land
Your [Am]love and [E7]good-will [Am]for to have
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

# Transpose the whole song at render time, e.g. up 3 semitones to Cm:
#   chordpro -x 3 -o greensleeves.pdf example-greensleeves.cho
# ...or per-song with a {transpose: 3} directive near the top.
